(in-ns 'go.arbace.py) ^{:go/comments [[5 1 "// Frames and threads (doc/python/PYI-SPEC.md §7.4; PYS7 (a)): a frame is a heap object holding a code"] [6 1 "// object's locals, cells, value stack and instruction index; the dispatch loop (eval.go) runs a"] [7 1 "// thread's frames without holding them on Go's stack, so a call from Python to Python is a new frame"] [8 1 "// and a return pops it, and a generator (PY5d) is a frame kept between resumptions."] [10 1 "// Frame is an executing code object (CPython's _PyInterpreterFrame and frame object)."] [13 21 "// the function run, nil for a module's or class's body"] [16 2 "// GlobalsMap is the globals when they are a dict subclass's instance (a function's from FunctionType(code, globals),"] [17 2 "// exec's and eval's; queue 205f), Globals its dict: LOAD_GLOBAL goes through its __getitem__; nil for a dict"] [19 19 "// the namespace of a module's or class's body (a module's is its Globals)"] [20 2 "// LocalsMap is a class body's namespace when __prepare__ returned a dict subclass: the name"] [21 2 "// operations go through its __getitem__, __setitem__ and __delitem__ (CPython's STORE_NAME on a"] [22 2 "// non-exact dict), Locals its dict. Added by PY5e as the integration's owner (part 2b: enum's"] [23 2 "// EnumDict)."] [25 21 "// the fast locals; nil is unbound"] [26 21 "// the cells, then the free variables' cells"] [28 16 "// the next instruction"] [29 16 "// the instruction running, or the last run (f_lasti; tracebacks' line)"] [31 2 "// Suspended is set by a yield (PY5d): the frame returned a value but is kept to be resumed."] [33 17 "// the loop returns when this frame returns: it was called from Go"] [34 2 "// reraisedAt and reraisedLasti: a reraise N set the frame's reported instruction back to the raise it"] [35 2 "// re-raises (RERAISE's oparg: frame->instr_ptr), while its handler is still looked up at the reraise"] [37 2 "// escaped: a Python object may hold the frame (sys._getframe, a traceback, gi_frame, f_back, a signal"] [38 2 "// handler's argument), so it is never reused (202b: releaseFrame)"] [40 2 "// initSelf: the frame is an __init__ callInit runs for a class's call (queue 210), the instance made"] [44 1 "// escape marks f and the frames its f_back reaches escaped (a frame a Python object may hold; 202b)."] [51 1 "// The frames of a function's calls are reused (202b: CPython allocates its frames in a per-thread stack): a frame"] [52 1 "// that returned, made by newFrame for a function that is not a generator or a coroutine, and that no Python object"] [53 1 "// can reach (not escaped) goes back to its code's free list, at most frameFreeMax of them, cleared; newFrame takes"] [54 1 "// one from there before it allocates."] [65 1 "// releaseGenFrame is releaseFrame for the frame of a generator, coroutine or async generator that returned (gen.go's"] [66 1 "// resume; queue 210): its object no longer holds it."] [82 1 "// FrameType is the frame objects' type (sys._getframe, a traceback's tb_frame)."] [87 1 "// Line is the frame's current line (f_lineno), 0 when the code has no lines."] [90 1 "// ReportedLasti is f_lasti: Lasti, or after a reraise N there the instruction it re-raises from."] [110 1 "// popN pops n items and returns them in stack order (a view, valid until the next push)."] [121 1 "// Thread is a Python thread's state (PyThreadState): its current frame, the exception being"] [122 1 "// handled (sys.exception()), the call depth against the recursion limit. One thread runs at a time"] [123 1 "// (the GIL: PYS10 (a), PY6)."] [127 17 "// the exception being handled at this level (None outside handlers): the frame's or generator's slot"] [128 2 "// outer are the slots of the levels a running generator or coroutine was resumed from (CPython's exc_info"] [129 2 "// stack, gi_exc_state's previous_item): sys.exception() is the first that is not None (CurrentHandled)"] [132 2 "// cdepth is the C level's depth (PY7): the nested built-in calls CPython guards by _Py_EnterRecursiveCall"] [133 2 "// (comparison, repr, str, a tuple's hash, isinstance's and issubclass's recursions, the eval loop entered from"] [134 2 "// C), which CPython 3.14 measures on the machine's stack and pyi counts (enterRecursiveCall)"] [136 26 "// the containers being repr'd (Py_ReprEnter)"] [137 26 "// callStack's signal, reused (202b)"] [140 1 "// CurrentHandled is the exception being handled (_PyErr_GetTopmostException): this level's slot, else the"] [141 1 "// first not None of the levels it was resumed from; None when none is."] [154 1 "// chainContext is _PyErr_SetObject's implicit chaining: exc's __context__ the exception being handled, a cycle"] [155 1 "// through exc in that chain cut first."] [173 10 "// a cycle not through exc"] [183 1 "// reprEnter is Py_ReprEnter: true when o is already being repr'd (a recursive container: \"[...]\")."] [195 1 "// reprLeave is Py_ReprLeave."] [198 1 "// The C level's stack (PY7). CPython 3.14 raises RecursionError \"Stack overflow (used N kB)WHERE\" when a guarded"] [199 1 "// built-in call (_Py_EnterRecursiveCall) finds the machine's stack past its soft limit; a Python frame does not use it."] [200 1 "// pyi's built-ins recurse on Go's stack, a goroutine's at most 1 GB, which a deep enough structure overflowed (a fatal"] [201 1 "// Go error: test_tuple's test_hash_deeply_nested, test_copy's reflexive comparisons, test_isinstance's recursions)."] [202 1 "// pyi counts the guarded levels instead, and Go's calls into the machine (Thread.run: the eval loop entered from C,"] [203 1 "// where \"\"): cStackLevels of them, cFrameBytes each as the message's nominal kB (about"] [204 1 "// CPython's 1 MB soft limit on Linux); CPython's own depth varies with the call (on Alpine aarch64 a tuple's hash"] [205 1 "// reaches 10,000 levels, its repr not)."] [211 1 "// enterRecursiveCall is _Py_EnterRecursiveCall(where): false, with the RecursionError, past the limit; else the"] [212 1 "// level is entered and leaveRecursiveCall leaves it."] [225 1 "// stackOverflow is _Py_CheckRecursiveCall's RecursionError."] [230 1 "// leaveRecursiveCall is _Py_LeaveRecursiveCall for enterRecursiveCall's thread."] [239 1 "// currentThread is the running thread (the GIL's holder)."] [242 1 "// unbound is the marker :load-fast-and-clear pushes for an unbound local (PEP 709)."] [249 1 "// newFrame makes the frame of a function's call with its arguments bound (CPython's"] [250 1 "// _PyEval_MakeFrameVector); args holds the positional then the keyword arguments."] [261 3 "// the fast locals and the value stack in one allocation (202b): the stack's room the most the code's"] [262 3 "// frames have needed (Code.stackHint, kept by runFrames at a return), so a call does not grow it from nothing"] [287 1 "// bindArgs puts a call's arguments into the parameters' slots (positional, *args, keyword-only,"] [288 1 "// **kwargs, then the defaults), raising CPython's TypeErrors (Python/ceval.c's, with the qualified name)."] [403 1 "// joinNames is CPython's list of names: 'a', 'a' and 'b', 'a', 'b', and 'c'."] [428 1 "// newGeneratorHook makes the generator, coroutine or async generator object of a call's frame (its"] [429 1 "// code flagged :generator or :coroutine): PY5d's gen.go sets it."] [432 1 "// callFunction calls a Python function from Go: a frame run by a nested loop to its return."]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[46 6] [46 30] [114 12] [114 30] [146 27] [146 35] [147 21] [254 21] [267 47] [270 37] [319 21] [319 43] [331 15] [331 30] [342 26] [356 19] [356 41] [373 28] [373 41] [380 12] [380 25] [389 18] [389 40]]} (go/file "frame.go" :imports [

